NAME
    cd - change the working directory

SYNOPSIS
    cd [DIR]

DESCRIPTION
    Make DIR the shell's working directory. With no argument, go to the
    root, /. DIR may be absolute or relative; "." and ".." are resolved by
    the shell before anything is asked of the filesystem.

    The new directory is walked from the root by its absolute path, never
    from the old working directory. A shell that walks by capability holds
    one capability for its working directory; walking from the root is what
    lets it give the old one back without losing the new one.

    A path that does not name a directory leaves the working directory
    where it was and reports "not a directory".

SEE ALSO
    pwd(1), ls(1), sh(1)
